evidence.summary:
The paced run covered all 52 v0.1 S1-S3 tests (CLM-0007 to 0027 and 0033 to 0063). 26 passed and 26 failed, and none ended at capacity. The paced run's one readiness label was clm_0150, which isn't v0.1. That includes the five tests EVD-0128 named as capacity-masked in M1:
- CLM-0042, 0052 and 0057 pass;
- CLM-0056 fails on #687;
- CLM-0061 fails on #687, with #682 and #688.

All 26 failures are filed sandbawks defects: #664, #665, #667, #675 to #679, #681, #682, #684, #687, #688, and #690 (new in M4, for CLM-0010 and CLM-0025). Each of the 26 tests passes on hosted E2B, so none is a crate bug.

The workflow_dispatch-only job "Live (hosted E2B)" reads the repository secret E2B_API_KEY_HOSTED on the three steps that need it and runs `just test-live hosted`. Its first run, on main at d9c6401, concluded success:
- 81 live tests: 78 passed, 3 volume tests skipped (volumes not enabled for the team), 0 failed;
- all three sweeps reported 0 leftovers;
- the log-key check passed and the log was uploaded as the live-hosted-log artifact.

With SnapshotMode::Filesystem, the result depends on the API's answer:
- a 409 whose message says "is already paused" gives Ok(false);
- a 409 with another message gives Error::Api with status 409 and that message;
- a 409 with no body gives Error::Api with status 409;
- a 400 gives Error::Api with status 400;
- a 404 gives SandboxNotFound.

SnapshotMode::Full reads the 409 body the same way. A pause without a mode treats any 409 as Ok(false), as SDK 2.61 does.

A mocked ListDir returns four entries:
- a link with isSymlink true and type FILE;
- an old-shape entry with type FILE_TYPE_SYMLINK;
- a plain file with isSymlink false;
- a directory link with isSymlink true.

list reports Symlink, Symlink, File and Symlink. get_info on the new-shape link reports Symlink and its symlink_target.

The file asserts at compile time that the following are Send + Sync:
- Client, ConnectionConfig and its builder;
- Sandbox, Commands, Pty, Filesystem and Volume;
- every options type and result type.

It also asserts that the stream handles are Send, that every public type is Debug, and that Error is a std::error::Error + Send + Sync + 'static. It compiles and passes on main.
